rived from the port's actual dispatch dynamics, two instrumented VM iterations): a C-LOOK tree dispatch removes its victim from the sector tree but leaves the node in the FIFO marked stale; when the victim IS the FIFO front (ascending arrivals), the next continuation dispatch call is consumed by the stale-front scavenge (lane_collect_stale_front + gc_has_work return-0) and the kernel falls back to the evacuate hook (scx_io_dispatch_request), which dispatches without any dir/batching/starved state \u2014 so under ascending arrivals the direction-selection state machine never advances under load and the starvation flip is unreachable no matter how deep the backlog is (measured: sel_mixed=0 with a 420-deep mixed queue). With DESCENDING arrivals the sweep victim is never the FIFO front, the continuation runs clean (batching++ every dispatch), a selection runs every 16 dispatches, and once the writes arrive (submitted last) the selections are mixed: starved 0->1->2, the 3rd evaluates >=2 -> FLIP to the write lane -> one contiguous ascending write epoch -> write-empty selection returns to reads with NO reset -> ascending read suffix. 128KB sizing: completion (~64us) is 10x+ the per-SQE submission cost (~3-5us measured), so the ~256 virtio driver tags saturate mid-submission and the mixed scheduler backlog reaches hundreds. Pre-saturation (~256-330 arrivals) dispatches immediately in DESCENDING order (unasserted prefix); the ascending sweep + flip + suffix is the asserted part."}